<sys/io.h> is an x86-only glibc header (inb/outb port I/O).  On aarch64 and
armv7 it does not exist, and emuscv does not use anything from it -- the
include is unconditional in the non-Windows, non-macOS branch.  Same fix as
batocera's 003-remove-io-header.patch, kept as a comment rather than a delete
so the next upstream rebase shows what was dropped.

